      "id": "uyz3x61",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to High Courts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Articles 214 to 231 in Part VI of the Constitution govern the organization, independence, jurisdiction, powers, and procedures of High Courts in India.",
        "The Chief Justice and other judges of a High Court are appointed by the President of India.",
        "A High Court judge holds office until attaining the age of 62 years and submits resignation directly to the President.",
        "Under Article 226, High Courts possess the power to issue writs for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights as well as for ordinary legal rights."
      ],
      "id": "s64tl72"
    },
